es for quick kingside castling and supports potential e4-d4 expansion.\n- It avoids passive development like Bc1-d2 or Qd1-d2, which don’t add immediate pressure.\n\nReason:  \nDeveloping the knight to f3 challenges Black’s centralized knight on e5 immediately, promotes rapid development, and supports White’s central control. It’s consistent with opening principles: develop knights before bishops, control the center, and avoid unnecessary pawn moves.\n\nAnswer: N: g1-f3"}
