White hasn't castled yet — so quick development is key.\n\nThus, best move is **B: g5-f4** — active development, good diagonal, no risk.\n\nReason: Developing the bishop to f4 increases pressure in the center, avoids premature exchanges, and supports future central control or kingside play. It's one of the most active and safe moves available.\n\nAnswer: B: g5-f4"}
